Here are the CRUD APIs for your Order project that work in both Swagger and Postman.

Assume your application is running on:

http://localhost:8080
1. Save Order (POST)
----------------------
URL
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
JSON Body
{
    "name":"Laptop",
    "cost":55000,
    "description":"Dell Inspiron 15"
}
Response
{
    "id":1,
    "name":"Laptop",
    "cost":55000.0,
    "description":"Dell Inspiron 15"
}
2. Get All Orders (GET)
------------------------
URL
GET http://localhost:8080/orders
Response
[
    {
        "id":1,
        "name":"Laptop",
        "cost":55000,
        "description":"Dell Inspiron 15"
    },
    {
        "id":2,
        "name":"Mobile",
        "cost":25000,
        "description":"Samsung"
    }
]
3. Get Order By ID (GET)
--------------------------
URL
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/1
Response
{
    "id":1,
    "name":"Laptop",
    "cost":55000,
    "description":"Dell Inspiron 15"
}
4. Update Order (PUT)
------------------------
URL
PUT http://localhost:8080/orders/1
JSON Body
{
    "name":"Gaming Laptop",
    "cost":75000,
    "description":"HP Victus"
}
Response
{
    "id":1,
    "name":"Gaming Laptop",
    "cost":75000,
    "description":"HP Victus"
}
5. Delete Order (DELETE)
-------------------------
URL
DELETE http://localhost:8080/orders/1
Response
Order Deleted Successfully...

Swagger APIs
-----------------------------
Open:

http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html

or

http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html

You will see:

Method	URL	Description
POST	/orders	Save Order
GET	/orders	Get All Orders
GET	/orders/{id}	Get Order By ID
PUT	/orders/{id}	Update Order
DELETE	/orders/{id}	Delete Order

Postman Collection
-----------------------
Method	URL	Body Required
POST	http://localhost:8080/orders	✅ Yes (JSON)
GET	http://localhost:8080/orders	❌ No
GET	http://localhost:8080/orders/1	❌ No
PUT	http://localhost:8080/orders/1	✅ Yes (JSON)
DELETE	http://localhost:8080/orders/1	❌ No

JSON for POST
{
    "name":"Laptop",
    "cost":55000,
    "description":"Dell Inspiron"
}
JSON for PUT
{
    "name":"Gaming Laptop",
    "cost":75000,
    "description":"HP Victus"
}

These same endpoints can be tested in Swagger UI (using Try it out) or in Postman by selecting the appropriate HTTP method and URL.
